1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,280
This syringe holds brown nitrogen dioxide,

2
00:00:03,360 --> 00:00:06,720
NO₂, mixed with colourless N₂O₄.

3
00:00:06,800 --> 00:00:08,320
It has sat at the same shade for

4
00:00:08,400 --> 00:00:11,360
an hour, so it is a dynamic equilibrium,

5
00:00:11,480 --> 00:00:13,600
and none of the gas can escape.

6
00:00:13,680 --> 00:00:16,400
Now we push the plunger
in slowly, squeezing

7
00:00:16,440 --> 00:00:18,640
the gas into half the space, and let

8
00:00:18,680 --> 00:00:20,400
it return to room temperature.

9
00:00:20,720 --> 00:00:22,000
Watch the colour.

10
00:00:22,080 --> 00:00:24,840
It darkens at once, then slowly fades a

11
00:00:24,880 --> 00:00:27,040
little, and it settles
darker than where it

12
00:00:27,120 --> 00:00:28,240
started.

13
00:00:28,320 --> 00:00:31,360
So why darker, why the fade, and does

14
00:00:31,520 --> 00:00:33,200
every rise in pressure do this?

15
00:00:34,434 --> 00:00:36,793
Here is the syringe at equilibrium, on a

16
00:00:36,834 --> 00:00:37,713
made-up scale.

17
00:00:38,274 --> 00:00:41,073
Concentration means how crowded a gas is.

18
00:00:41,634 --> 00:00:43,953
NO₂ is eight units and

19
00:00:44,034 --> 00:00:45,753
N₂O₄ is four.

20
00:00:46,114 --> 00:00:48,913
Joining, two NO₂ into one

21
00:00:48,994 --> 00:00:51,473
N₂O₄, is the forward reaction, and

22
00:00:51,554 --> 00:00:53,073
splitting is the reverse.

23
00:00:53,714 --> 00:00:56,273
Both rates are thirty-two,
so the amounts are

24
00:00:56,354 --> 00:00:56,913
steady.

25
00:00:58,134 --> 00:00:59,653
Now we halve the volume.

26
00:01:00,054 --> 00:01:02,693
The same particles have half the room, so

27
00:01:02,774 --> 00:01:06,053
every concentration doubles: NO₂ goes from

28
00:01:06,214 --> 00:01:08,853
eight to sixteen, and N₂O₄

29
00:01:09,014 --> 00:01:10,533
from four to eight.

30
00:01:10,934 --> 00:01:13,333
Nothing has reacted yet, but the brown is

31
00:01:13,574 --> 00:01:15,893
already darker, because NO₂ is the

32
00:01:15,974 --> 00:01:17,013
brown gas.

33
00:01:18,234 --> 00:01:19,273
Now the rates.

34
00:01:19,834 --> 00:01:22,553
Joining needs two NO₂ to meet,

35
00:01:22,634 --> 00:01:25,113
and each one is twice as crowded, so

36
00:01:25,194 --> 00:01:28,793
joining speeds up twice
over: thirty-two times two

37
00:01:28,874 --> 00:01:31,713
times two is one hundred and twenty-eight.

38
00:01:32,074 --> 00:01:34,713
Splitting needs only one N₂O₄,

39
00:01:34,794 --> 00:01:37,433
so it only doubles, to sixty-four.

40
00:01:37,474 --> 00:01:41,033
The squeeze boosts both
reactions, but joining gains

41
00:01:41,114 --> 00:01:41,593
more.

42
00:01:42,800 --> 00:01:45,600
Joining is now faster, so more

43
00:01:45,680 --> 00:01:48,160
NO₂ is lost each second than is rebuilt,

44
00:01:48,240 --> 00:01:49,920
and the brown starts to fade.

45
00:01:50,560 --> 00:01:52,720
Two NO₂ join into one

46
00:01:52,760 --> 00:01:54,720
N₂O₄, so the number of gas

47
00:01:54,800 --> 00:01:56,000
particles falls.

48
00:01:56,640 --> 00:01:59,040
One joining step later, NO₂ has

49
00:01:59,120 --> 00:02:01,680
fallen to fourteen and N₂O₄

50
00:02:01,760 --> 00:02:03,320
has risen to nine.

51
00:02:03,760 --> 00:02:05,600
Joining depends on the NO₂ count

52
00:02:05,760 --> 00:02:08,240
twice over, so it slows from one hundred

53
00:02:08,320 --> 00:02:10,720
and twenty-eight to ninety-eight.

54
00:02:10,880 --> 00:02:12,720
Splitting depends on the N₂O₄

55
00:02:12,960 --> 00:02:15,800
count once, so it rises from sixty-four to

56
00:02:15,840 --> 00:02:17,120
seventy-two.

57
00:02:17,160 --> 00:02:19,440
The difference between
the rates is closing.

58
00:02:20,667 --> 00:02:24,026
Then the rates meet again,
at about seventy-eight.

59
00:02:24,107 --> 00:02:25,906
NO₂ settles at about twelve and

60
00:02:25,947 --> 00:02:26,786
a half.

61
00:02:27,067 --> 00:02:28,986
That is between the eight we started with

62
00:02:29,147 --> 00:02:32,026
and the sixteen straight
after the squeeze, which

63
00:02:32,107 --> 00:02:33,826
is why the brown ends darker than the

64
00:02:33,867 --> 00:02:37,386
start, but paler than
right after the squeeze.

65
00:02:37,507 --> 00:02:40,106
Both rates are higher than
before, because everything

66
00:02:40,187 --> 00:02:41,466
is more crowded.

67
00:02:41,547 --> 00:02:43,786
The mixture has shifted
to the right, toward

68
00:02:43,867 --> 00:02:46,346
N₂O₄, and it only partly

69
00:02:46,427 --> 00:02:47,626
cancelled the squeeze.

70
00:02:48,834 --> 00:02:51,713
At the moment of the squeeze,
both concentrations

71
00:02:51,794 --> 00:02:54,993
jump together, and both
rates step up, joining

72
00:02:55,074 --> 00:02:55,633
by more.

73
00:02:56,194 --> 00:02:59,473
Then the reaction responds: NO₂ slides

74
00:02:59,554 --> 00:03:02,353
down, N₂O₄ creeps up, and

75
00:03:02,434 --> 00:03:03,473
the rates meet.

76
00:03:04,700 --> 00:03:06,860
So why did joining gain more?

77
00:03:07,340 --> 00:03:09,980
Because it depends on more gas particles.

78
00:03:10,220 --> 00:03:11,260
That gives a rule.

79
00:03:11,740 --> 00:03:14,220
A squeeze speeds up most the reaction that

80
00:03:14,420 --> 00:03:17,100
depends on more gas
particles, so the shift

81
00:03:17,180 --> 00:03:19,740
goes toward the side
with fewer gas particles.

82
00:03:20,300 --> 00:03:21,900
Count only the gases.

83
00:03:22,300 --> 00:03:24,380
Chemists say moles of gas.

84
00:03:24,780 --> 00:03:26,780
It is the same count: the numbers in

85
00:03:26,900 --> 00:03:29,220
front of the gases
in the balanced equation.

86
00:03:29,500 --> 00:03:33,020
In nitrogen plus three
hydrogen making two ammonia,

87
00:03:33,060 --> 00:03:35,020
there are four gas particles on the left

88
00:03:35,180 --> 00:03:37,260
and two on the right, so the forward

89
00:03:37,340 --> 00:03:40,220
reaction depends on more
gas particles and gains

90
00:03:40,300 --> 00:03:40,700
more.

91
00:03:41,180 --> 00:03:42,780
Squeezing shifts it right.

92
00:03:43,260 --> 00:03:45,900
Expanding does the opposite,
so the shift goes

93
00:03:45,980 --> 00:03:48,460
toward the side with more gas particles.

94
00:03:49,667 --> 00:03:51,666
What if both sides have the same number

95
00:03:51,747 --> 00:03:53,066
of gas particles?

96
00:03:53,347 --> 00:03:56,786
Take hydrogen plus purple
iodine vapour making two

97
00:03:56,947 --> 00:04:00,866
colourless hydrogen iodide,
as hot gases: two against

98
00:04:00,947 --> 00:04:01,266
two.

99
00:04:01,747 --> 00:04:05,586
A squeeze doubles every
concentration, and both reactions

100
00:04:05,667 --> 00:04:08,386
need two particles to meet, so both rates

101
00:04:08,467 --> 00:04:11,026
go up four times and stay equal.

102
00:04:11,107 --> 00:04:13,106
The gas is more crowded and the purple

103
00:04:13,187 --> 00:04:15,426
is darker, but nothing shifts.

104
00:04:16,634 --> 00:04:19,753
Pure solids and pure liquids do not count,

105
00:04:19,874 --> 00:04:21,993
because squeezing does
not make them any more

106
00:04:22,074 --> 00:04:22,873
crowded.

107
00:04:23,194 --> 00:04:26,633
So in solid carbon plus
carbon dioxide making

108
00:04:26,714 --> 00:04:30,553
two carbon monoxide,
only the gases count: one

109
00:04:30,634 --> 00:04:32,393
on the left, two on the right.

110
00:04:32,954 --> 00:04:35,753
The same rule applies:
a squeeze favours the

111
00:04:35,834 --> 00:04:38,553
side with fewer gas
particles, so it shifts

112
00:04:38,634 --> 00:04:39,113
left.

113
00:04:40,334 --> 00:04:43,133
A squeeze raises the total
pressure, because the

114
00:04:43,254 --> 00:04:46,093
crowded particles hit
the walls more often.

115
00:04:46,134 --> 00:04:49,133
But pressure can also
rise without a squeeze.

116
00:04:49,454 --> 00:04:51,653
Take our NO₂ syringe, lock the

117
00:04:51,694 --> 00:04:54,333
plunger so the volume
cannot change, and pump

118
00:04:54,414 --> 00:04:55,493
in argon.

119
00:04:55,854 --> 00:04:58,253
Argon is an inert gas, which means it

120
00:04:58,414 --> 00:05:00,253
takes no part in the reaction.

121
00:05:00,574 --> 00:05:02,013
But the NO₂ and the

122
00:05:02,094 --> 00:05:03,853
N₂O₄ have the same room as

123
00:05:04,094 --> 00:05:06,893
before, so each is exactly as crowded as

124
00:05:06,974 --> 00:05:07,733
before.

125
00:05:08,094 --> 00:05:10,333
Argon does not crowd NO₂ any

126
00:05:10,414 --> 00:05:12,413
closer to N₂O₄, so it

127
00:05:12,494 --> 00:05:14,973
does not favour either
direction, and there is

128
00:05:15,054 --> 00:05:17,853
no shift and no colour change.

129
00:05:17,934 --> 00:05:20,333
A squeeze and an argon top-up can raise

130
00:05:20,414 --> 00:05:23,453
the total pressure equally,
but only the squeeze

131
00:05:23,574 --> 00:05:25,613
crowds the reacting gases.

132
00:05:25,654 --> 00:05:27,933
So total pressure by itself is not the

133
00:05:28,014 --> 00:05:28,973
cause.

134
00:05:29,134 --> 00:05:31,453
Crowding of the reacting gases is.

135
00:05:32,667 --> 00:05:34,746
Here is a shortcut for the direction.

136
00:05:34,987 --> 00:05:37,466
Squeeze it, and the shift
goes toward fewer

137
00:05:37,547 --> 00:05:38,706
gas particles.

138
00:05:38,987 --> 00:05:41,226
Argon added in a fixed box does not

139
00:05:41,307 --> 00:05:41,986
shift it.

140
00:05:42,187 --> 00:05:43,786
It gives the direction only.

141
00:05:44,267 --> 00:05:46,906
The reason is still how
crowded each reacting

142
00:05:46,987 --> 00:05:48,106
gas becomes.

143
00:05:49,334 --> 00:05:49,973
Your turn.

144
00:05:50,214 --> 00:05:53,333
In a cylinder with a piston,
colourless nitric

145
00:05:53,414 --> 00:05:57,013
oxide, NO, and colourless oxygen are in

146
00:05:57,134 --> 00:06:00,293
equilibrium with brown NO₂: two N

147
00:06:00,374 --> 00:06:03,253
O plus oxygen make two NO₂.

148
00:06:03,494 --> 00:06:05,013
The temperature stays steady.

149
00:06:05,414 --> 00:06:07,413
The cylinder is hot, so the

150
00:06:07,534 --> 00:06:10,133
NO₂ stays as single molecules and does not

151
00:06:10,214 --> 00:06:12,533
join to make N₂O₄.

152
00:06:12,694 --> 00:06:15,253
One: you push the piston in to halve

153
00:06:15,334 --> 00:06:15,973
the volume.

154
00:06:16,374 --> 00:06:18,693
Which way does the net reaction go, and

155
00:06:18,774 --> 00:06:19,173
why?

156
00:06:19,574 --> 00:06:21,733
What does the colour do straight away, and

157
00:06:21,814 --> 00:06:23,893
then once the mixture has settled again?

158
00:06:24,454 --> 00:06:27,493
Two: back at the original
equilibrium, you lock

159
00:06:27,534 --> 00:06:29,893
the piston and pump in argon until the

160
00:06:29,974 --> 00:06:31,653
total pressure doubles.

161
00:06:31,734 --> 00:06:33,413
What happens to the shift and to the

162
00:06:33,494 --> 00:06:35,093
colour, and why?

163
00:06:35,214 --> 00:06:37,173
Pause the video if you'd like more time.

164
00:06:47,600 --> 00:06:48,200
One.

165
00:06:48,400 --> 00:06:51,440
Count the gases: three
particles on the left,

166
00:06:51,520 --> 00:06:52,720
two on the right.

167
00:06:52,960 --> 00:06:55,640
A squeeze doubles every concentration.

168
00:06:55,920 --> 00:06:58,880
The forward reaction depends
on more gas particles,

169
00:06:58,960 --> 00:07:01,280
so it gains more, and the net reaction

170
00:07:01,360 --> 00:07:03,920
goes right, toward NO₂.

171
00:07:04,000 --> 00:07:06,160
The colour darkens at once, because the

172
00:07:06,240 --> 00:07:08,640
NO₂ is twice as crowded, and then

173
00:07:08,680 --> 00:07:11,040
keeps darkening as more NO₂ forms

174
00:07:11,120 --> 00:07:13,320
each second than is used up, until the

175
00:07:13,360 --> 00:07:15,040
rates match again.

176
00:07:15,160 --> 00:07:17,360
This time the brown does not fade, because

177
00:07:17,440 --> 00:07:19,840
the shift makes the brown gas.

178
00:07:19,920 --> 00:07:22,240
If you said the brown fades, check which

179
00:07:22,320 --> 00:07:23,920
side this shift favours.

180
00:07:25,134 --> 00:07:25,533
Two.

181
00:07:25,774 --> 00:07:28,573
Argon takes no part, and the volume has

182
00:07:28,654 --> 00:07:32,493
not changed, so nitric
oxide, oxygen and nitrogen

183
00:07:32,574 --> 00:07:36,013
dioxide are each exactly
as crowded as before.

184
00:07:36,654 --> 00:07:39,693
Argon does not favour
either direction, so nothing

185
00:07:39,774 --> 00:07:41,773
shifts and the colour stays the same.

186
00:07:42,414 --> 00:07:44,173
If you said it shifts right because the

187
00:07:44,254 --> 00:07:47,373
pressure doubled, separate
the total pressure from how

188
00:07:47,534 --> 00:07:49,453
crowded the reacting gases are.

189
00:07:50,667 --> 00:07:53,386
So when a question
changes the pressure, ask

190
00:07:53,547 --> 00:07:56,186
first whether the reacting
gases got more or

191
00:07:56,347 --> 00:07:57,466
less crowded.

192
00:07:57,787 --> 00:08:00,506
If the volume changed, they did, so count

193
00:08:00,547 --> 00:08:02,506
the gas particles on each side.

194
00:08:02,827 --> 00:08:06,346
A squeeze shifts toward
fewer, an expansion toward

195
00:08:06,507 --> 00:08:09,306
more, and equal counts mean no shift.

196
00:08:10,027 --> 00:08:11,626
If you added a reacting gas in a

197
00:08:11,707 --> 00:08:14,586
fixed box, that is the
concentration case from

198
00:08:14,627 --> 00:08:15,546
the iron tube.

199
00:08:16,187 --> 00:08:18,026
If you added only an inert gas in

200
00:08:18,067 --> 00:08:20,826
a fixed box, nothing is more crowded, so

201
00:08:21,067 --> 00:08:21,866
nothing shifts.

202
00:08:22,667 --> 00:08:24,826
Next: adding a catalyst.

